  "created": "2026-11-11T14:33:08.65Z",
  "description": "Roslyn analyzers enforcing opinionated .NET conventions at compile time. Code fixes for most rules, covering design (sealed-by-default, async void, sync-over-async, in-modifier safety, primary constructor fields, FileSystemInfo equality, TimeProvider, IHttpClientFactory, TimeSpan for durations, mutable collection exposure, DI registration, Task.Run async lambda, excessive inheritance, enum switch, List<T> as IReadOnlyList<T>, Dictionary<K,V> as IReadOnlyDictionary<K,V>, unused interface params, static readonly arrays as ImmutableArray, stale ReferenceAssemblies, readonly struct init, ByteSize for data-size values, ByteSize unwrap via cast), reliability (DateTime.Parse roundtrip, GeneratedRegex timeout/backtracking, hardcoded /tmp paths, Task.FromResult sync I/O, Task.WhenAll unbounded/cancellation, JsonDocument lifetime, concurrency limits, catch filter OCE, options bind init, HttpClient missing OCE catch, FileInfo.Exists TOCTOU, unprotected finally cleanup, disk write-then-read round-trip, pool capacity guard, QuerySelectorAll materialization, TextContent length guard, GetAttribute element type, CompositeDetection specificity, sync local function call), performance (MinBy/MaxBy, HttpCompletionOption, string interpolation, ToArray in foreach, FrozenSet allocation, multi-string OR-chain, static readonly frozen collections, loop complexity, SHA256.HashData, StringBuilderPool), security (FIPS-approved hash algorithms, insecure Random in crypto context), style (string.Empty, Encoding.UTF8, XML doc comments, temp path conventions, null-forgiving operator, suppression audit, pragma balance, IDE1006 naming rule fix), and testing (temp directory cleanup, stale ReferenceAssemblies, Trait category). Both assemblies target netstandard2.0 and the package declares no dependencies, so one build loads in a .NET 11 host.",
  "developmentDependency": true,
